-- title:
--   Proposition 2.7 (Brion) for an integral simplex — the exponential sum is the sum of the vertex cone contributions
-- statement:
--   Let $v_1,\dots,v_{k+1}\in\mathbb{Z}^d$ be affinely independent and $\Delta=\operatorname{conv}\{v_1,\dots,v_{k+1}\}$ the integral simplex they span. For a vertex $v_j$, let $K_{v_j}$ be the cone generated by the edge vectors $v_i-v_j$ ($i\ne j$), with $\sigma(K_{v_j};c)$ given by the closed form for these generators. Then for every $c\in\mathbb{R}^d$ that is not a singular point of any $\sigma(K_{v_j};\cdot)$, i.e. $\langle c,v_i-v_j\rangle\ne0$ for all $i\ne j$,
--   $$\sum_{x\in\Delta\cap\mathbb{Z}^d}\exp\{\langle c,x\rangle\}=\sum_{j=1}^{k+1}\exp\{\langle c,v_j\rangle\}\cdot\sigma(K_{v_j};c).$$
--
--   Brion's identity reduces counting lattice points in a polytope to the generating functions of its vertex cones; Barvinok's algorithm evaluates its right-hand side through the constant terms of the cone functions.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper states Proposition 2.7 for every integral polytope. It is stated here for integral simplices, the only case the proof of Theorem 1.2 uses: for a general polytope the vertex cones need not be simple, and the paper gives no closed form of $\sigma$ for non-simple cones. The generators of $K_{v_j}$ are the edge vectors, as in Definition 2.6 ("$K_v$ is generated by the vectors $w-v$"). The left side is a finite sum.
-- source:
--   Barvinok, A polynomial time algorithm for counting integral points in polyhedra when the dimension is fixed, Math. Oper. Res. 19 (1994), p. 771, Proposition 2.7 (Brion 1988, 1992), specialized to integral simplices

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BarvinokCount_ShortFormula_sigma
import Definitions.Def_BarvinokCount_ShortFormula_integralSimplex

namespace BarvinokCount.ShortFormula

theorem brion_simplex {d k : ℕ} (v : Fin (k + 1) → Fin d → ℤ)
    (hv : AffineIndependent ℝ fun j => castVec (v j))
    (c : Fin d → ℝ) (hc : ∀ j, IsRegular (edgeGens v j) c) :
    ∑ᶠ z ∈ {z : Fin d → ℤ | castVec z ∈ simplex v}, Real.exp (c ⬝ᵥ castVec z) =
      ∑ j, Real.exp (c ⬝ᵥ castVec (v j)) * sigma (edgeGens v j) c := by sorry

end BarvinokCount.ShortFormula
